; Boss16_Kangaroo_XAU_21_30_scaled_demo.set - ORDER-190 demo candidate.
; Base = Boss16_Kangaroo_XAU_21_30.set (ORDER-077 candidate, RSI 21/30 fixed) with
; _16_BaseLotMode flipped to 1 (balance-scaled) instead of 0 (flat). Everything else
; byte-identical to the flat baseline.
;
; Anchor choice (user 2026-07-24: "เปิดบน demo ก่อน ไม่แตะ live"): _43_BalanceAnchor=10000
; matches the deposit val078/21_30 was validated at, and _43_LotPerAnchor=0.01 matches
; _16_BaseLot below -- so at the SAME $10,000 starting balance this config trades the
; IDENTICAL first lot as the flat baseline (0.01). It only diverges as balance moves away
; from $10,000: grows proportionally if balance rises, shrinks (self-attenuating toward
; hard-kill per ORDER-188 evidence) if balance falls. This is a deliberate choice, not the
; compiled default (_43_BalanceAnchor=1000 would silently 10x the lot at a $10k deposit --
; see mm_lotmode_test.ps1 K1_scaled_1x case, which exercises exactly that default and is
; correct FOR THAT TEST but wrong for an apples-to-apples demo vs flat).
;
; NOT attached anywhere yet -- Boss_16_KangarooGrid has no row in DEPLOYMENTS.csv (chassis
; has never been deployed live or demo). This .set is PENDING_ATTACH: user opens a demo
; MT5, drags Boss_16_KangarooGrid.ex5 onto an XAUUSD H1 chart, loads this .set. Once
; attached, re-pin this exact .set + first-tick log as the baseline and log the account/
; magic into DEPLOYMENTS.csv in the same session (taskboard convention).
;
; Regression note: tpl_regression.ps1 is unaffected (mode 0 default untouched, CLEAN 8/8
; per ORDER-190 log). mm_lotmode_test.ps1 K0/K1 cases (2026-07-24 re-run) confirm the
; _16_BaseLotMode=1 mechanism itself is CLEAN (deposit-invariance + unit-independence PASS).
;
